WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:03.852
Unit twenty-one. How the Internet Works!

2
00:00:04.795 --> 00:00:09.675
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emily, your technology teacher.

3
00:00:09.725 --> 00:00:12.638
Hi, Ms. Emily! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:12.688 --> 00:00:16.670
Today we learn about How the Internet Works. Let's go!

5
00:00:17.809 --> 00:00:21.733
Internet. Say it with me. Internet!

6
00:00:25.233 --> 00:00:29.191
Packets. Say it with me. Packets!

7
00:00:32.662 --> 00:00:36.529
Router. Say it with me. Router!

8
00:00:40.008 --> 00:00:43.664
Server. Say it with me. Server!

9
00:00:47.222 --> 00:00:50.948
Cable. Say it with me. Cable!

10
00:00:54.433 --> 00:00:58.298
Data. Say it with me. Data!

11
00:01:01.812 --> 00:01:06.165
Address. Say it with me. Address!

12
00:01:09.667 --> 00:01:13.908
Network. Say it with me. Network!

13
00:01:17.405 --> 00:01:30.934
The internet is a giant network of computers. Data is split into small packets that travel through a router and cable to a server. Each device has an address so packets arrive in the right place.

14
00:01:30.984 --> 00:01:34.405
Now I understand. Thank you, Ms. Emily!

15
00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:40.496
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:40.546 --> 00:01:41.696
Router!

17
00:01:42.675 --> 00:01:48.281
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:48.331 --> 00:01:49.481
Address!

19
00:01:50.453 --> 00:01:56.386
Did you know? Most internet data between continents travels through cables under the sea!

20
00:01:56.436 --> 00:01:58.650
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:01:59.701 --> 00:02:08.586
Think and answer. How does a message travel across the internet?

22
00:02:08.636 --> 00:02:09.818
Great answer!

23
00:02:10.775 --> 00:02:16.553
Great job today! Keep learning, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
